text \<open>\<^bold>\<open>Known divergence from Mojo.\<close> Mojo destroys the fields of a 'deinit self' individually, as soon as they are no longer needed; fields that __deinit__ never mentions are destroyed on entry, before its body runs. The model destroys all fields after the body.
  The lemma below asserts that the semantics does NOT yet reproduce the compiler's behaviour; when the semantics is fixed it will fail and should be turned into a normal test (remove the entry from known_divergences.json).\<close>

lemma t_d05_nested_fields_diverges: \<open>\<not> test_output t_d05_nested_fields 5000 [''drop inner 1'', ''drop inner 2'', ''drop outer 9'', ''built'']\<close>
  by eval

